{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3062","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3062","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3062\",\"parent_revision\":\"9c9a4e466cac860936719d5c02443f9c4f2dad30\",\"root_revision\":\"102440addc9a419a63baa60a413099cc9290783896aaa5a06f9d270b240745d5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPagination has no content identity. Page structures carry a page number and total, but nothing identifying which document they page. Across stateless invocations a caller cannot request \\\"the next page of what you just returned\\\" \u2014 every page request re-collects from the provider and re-parses.\\n\\nThis is also a correctness gap: if content changes between page requests, pages from two different versions can be returned as though they were one document.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:11:49.444303Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: feat: address paginated content by content identity\\nDate: 2026-08-20\\nGoal: Implement the content-identity-addressed control set (R8 of the markdown-consumption contract) so paginated/navigable responses are addressable and re-servable without re-collecting from source or redoing Generation, per ADR-3082-1's finalized design.\\nConditions:\\n1. content_id derivation rule (command + Generation output binding, not raw source or generated content alone) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Storage schema (content_id PK, source, command, content, stale marker, timestamps) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Storage location convention (state_root()/control-set.db, WAL mode) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Eviction/cleanup policy parameters (40MB soft target, LRU-by-size, periodic rate-limited hourly-to-daily sweep) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Which existing write paths across the codebase must trigger invalidation (marking a matching content_id stale) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n6. Where the Navigation stage currently lives in code (progressive_markdown package) and what wiring is needed to route through the new control set | Status: DERIVABLE\\n7. FileCache/GitHubContentCache boundary \u2014 confirmed unrelated to the control set, must not be conflated | Status: AVAILABLE\\n8. task_status_hook.py's exact current location and shape (flagged by cross-session review as a future required invalidation-trigger caller) | Status: MISSING\\n9. Concurrent-writer hardening scope confirmed deferred to #3081, not blocking this item's baseline single-writer path | Status: AVAILABLE\\n10. Existing test patterns for backend/provider code in this plugin to follow | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 1\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:17:40.282432Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: unbounded-design\\n\\n**Rationale**: Greenfield feature implementation with fully specified design. All design decisions finalized in merged ADRs (3075-1 through 3075-4, ADR-3082-1). Storage mechanism (SQLite at state_root()/control-set.db, WAL mode), content_id derivation rule (command + Generation output binding), eviction policy (40MB soft target, LRU-by-size, periodic sweep), and stale detection already decided. No unresolved design questions. RT-ICA snapshot shows 6 AVAILABLE conditions, 3 DERIVABLE (task_status_hook.py path location, existing test patterns), 1 MISSING (will be located during planning). Only code implementation work remains.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Read backlog item description, RT-ICA snapshot, feature-context artifact, teammate briefing context, and walked decision tree. Item explicitly stated as \\\"greenfield implementation of a new SQLite-backed content-identity control set \u2014 the design itself is already fully decided via 6 merged ADRs, only the code implementation remains.\\\"\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Implement SQLite-backed content identity control set per ADR-3082-1's finalized design \u2192 Enables pagination response reuse without re-collection/re-parsing and correctness improvement (prevents serving pages from different content versions as one document)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:18:27.441656Z</sub>\\n\\n## Codebase-side implementation research (wave 0)\\n\\nScope: where Navigation-stage code lives, which write paths need an invalidation hook, what\\n`state_root()` returns and how existing SQLite state follows (or doesn't follow) it, and what test\\npatterns exist for backend/provider/SQLite code in this plugin. Architecture (schema, eviction,\\n`content_id`) is already decided in ADR-3082-1 \u2014 this section only covers implementation-site facts.\\n\\n### Navigation stage location\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/progressive_markdown/` \u2014 package with `navigator.py` (`ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator`\\nfacade, 505 lines), `providers.py` (`MarkdownContentProvider` protocol + `CallableMarkdownContentProvider` +\\n`MCPMarkdownContentProvider`), plus `indexer.py`, `parser.py`, `pagination.py`, `list_navigator.py`,\\n`tokenizer.py`, `renderers.py`, `codeblocks.py`, `links.py`, `models.py`, `exceptions.py`.\\n\\n`ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator.load(source, **provider_kwargs)` (navigator.py) is the single chokepoint that\\ncalls the injected `provider.get_markdown()` (Collection), then `MarkdownItParser.parse()` + `MarkdownIndexer.build()`\\n(Generation), and stores the result on `self._document`. Every navigation method (`map`, `links`, `view_section`,\\n`view_code`, `search_sections`) reads `self._document` \u2014 none of them re-invoke `load()`. This means the control\\nset sits **between `load()`'s two halves**: a `content_id`-keyed read/write wraps the provider call + parse\\nstep, not the navigation methods themselves. `providers.py` has no state and nothing to change structurally \u2014\\n`MarkdownContentProvider` is a plain `Protocol`, so a control-set-aware provider or a wrapper around\\n`ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator.load()` are both viable insertion points; no existing hook for this exists yet.\\n\\nThere is no existing content-identity, caching, or SQLite code anywhere in `progressive_markdown/` \u2014 this is\\nwholly new code, not an extension of an existing mechanism in this package.\\n\\n### `dh_paths.py` \u2014 `state_root()` and the slug inconsistency\\n\\n`state_root(project_root=None)` returns `_dh_user_root() / \\\"projects\\\" / slug` where `slug = compute_slug(root)`\\nand `compute_slug()` is `str(project_root).replace(\\\"/\\\", \\\"-\\\")` \u2014 **no `.lstrip(\\\"/\\\")`**, so the slug keeps its\\nleading `-` (e.g. `-home-user-repos-claude_skills`). `_dh_user_root()` is `~/.dh` or `$DH_STATE_HOME`. Every\\nTier 2/3 directory helper (`backlog_dir`, `plan_dir`, `milestones_dir`, `research_dir`, `context_dir`,\\n`reports_dir`) is `state_root(project_root) / \\\"<name>\\\"` \u2014 no directory helper exists yet for a bare file\\n(no `*_db_path()` or equivalent). ADR-3082-1 requires `control-set.db` directly at `state_root()/control-set.db`,\\nso a new helper (e.g. `control_set_db_path()`) following the existing `*_dir()` pattern is needed, plus a\\n`Path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` on `state_root()` itself (already covered by `ensure_dirs()`, but that\\nfunction doesn't currently create a bare-file path, only directories).\\n\\n**Discovered inconsistency, relevant to placement:** the only existing SQLite state file in this plugin,\\n`dispatch-state.db`, does **not** use `dh_paths.state_root()`/`compute_slug()`. Both call sites\\n(`backlog_core/server.py::_project_stub()` and `dh_core/operations.py::_dispatch_db_path()`) independently\\ncompute `str(project_root).lstrip(\\\"/\\\").replace(\\\"/\\\", \\\"-\\\")` \u2014 **with** `.lstrip(\\\"/\\\")`, so the slug has **no**\\nleading dash, e.g. `home-user-repos-claude_skills`. This means `dispatch-state.db` currently lives in a\\nsibling-but-different directory (`~/.dh/projects/home-user-repos-claude_skills/dispatch-state.db`) than every\\nother Tier 2/3 state artifact (`~/.dh/projects/-home-user-repos-claude_skills/backlog/`, etc.) \u2014 a pre-existing\\ndrift, not something to replicate. ADR-3082-1 is explicit that `control-set.db` must nest under\\n`dh_paths.state_root()` (the `-`-prefixed slug), so implementation should call `dh_paths.state_root()` /\\n`dh_paths.compute_slug()` directly rather than following the `dispatch-state.db` call sites' local\\nreimplementation.\\n\\n### Existing SQLite pattern to follow: `DispatchStateManager`\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py` (`DispatchStateManager`, 741 lines) is the closest\\nprecedent \u2014 a synchronous, standalone (no MCP/FastMCP import) SQLite state manager taking a `db_path: Path` in\\n`__init__`, calling `sqlite3.connect(str(db_path), check_same_thread=False)`, `row_factory = sqlite3.Row`, then\\n`self.ensure_schema()` which runs an idempotent `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` / `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS`\\n`executescript()`. Async callers (`backlog_core/server.py`, `dh_core/operations.py`) wrap every call in\\n`asyncio.to_thread()`. This is a directly reusable shape for the control-set manager. Two gaps relative to\\nADR-3082-1's requirements: (1) `DispatchStateManager` does **not** set `PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL` anywhere \u2014 only\\n`backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py` (the 6-table work-item backend, explicitly *not* to be reused per the\\nADR's Consequences) sets `PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL` \u2014 so WAL-mode setup for `control-set.db` has no in-repo\\nprecedent to copy verbatim, it must be added fresh (`PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL` + `PRAGMA auto_vacuum=INCREMENTAL`\\nper the ADR); (2) neither existing SQLite manager wraps its write sequences in explicit transactions beyond\\nsqlite3's own autocommit-per-statement default \u2014 consistent with ADR-3082-1 deferring that to #3081.\\n\\n### Write paths needing an invalidation hook\\n\\nTwo async MCP servers hold every write path in this plugin that could invalidate a stored `content_id` entry:\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`: `backlog_add`, `backlog_update`, `backlog_groom`,\\n  `backlog_close`, `backlog_resolve`, `backlog_sync`, `backlog_strike_entry`, `backlog_update_sam_task_status`,\\n  `artifact_register` \u2014 every one of these mutates a backlog item, artifact, or GitHub-synced state that\\n  `backlog_view`/`artifact_read` (per ADR-3082-1, R8's stated future consumers) could have served through the\\n  control set.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py`: `sam_plan` (single dispatcher, `config.action` one of\\n  `read|create|list|status|ready|update|append_task|finalize`) and `sam_task` (single dispatcher, `config.action`\\n  one of `read|claim|state|update`) \u2014 the non-`read`/`list`/`status`/`ready` actions are the write paths.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` (996 lines): the\\n  confirmed external consumer named in Functional Requirement 8. This hook is a **separate `uv run --script`\\n  subprocess** per invocation (PEP 723, own interpreter) \u2014 it explicitly does **not** write task YAML directly\\n  (`ADR-001: hooks must not write directly to YAML`, stated in its module docstring); all writes route through\\n  `_call_sam_fastmcp()` (a `subprocess.run([..., \\\"fastmcp\\\", ...])` call) into the SAM MCP server itself. The two\\n  write-triggering call sites inside the hook are `_call_sam_task_state()` (task status write) and\\n  `_call_sam_task_update()` (task field write), both around line 452-500. Because this hook runs as an isolated\\n  subprocess with no shared Python state with the SAM server process, it cannot itself hold or import the\\n  control-set invalidation function's live state \u2014 it can only call an entrypoint that is itself\\n  out-of-process-safe (i.e., a plain function that opens the SQLite DB, marks rows stale, and closes it), which\\n  is exactly what ADR-3082-1's design already assumes (every access opens its own connection to one file). The\\n  natural call site is either directly inside this hook (after a successful `_call_sam_fastmcp` write) or inside\\n  `sam_schema/server.py`'s task-write handling that the hook's subprocess call reaches \u2014 both are valid; the\\n  hook's own subprocess isolation means whichever entrypoint is chosen must be importable/callable without\\n  requiring in-process server state.\\n\\n### Test patterns for backend/provider/SQLite code\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_state.py` (761 lines) is the direct precedent for testing a\\n  new control-set SQLite manager: one `tmp_path`-backed `DispatchStateManager` instantiated fresh per test (no\\n  shared fixture, no mutable shared state), grouped into `Test*` classes per concern (e.g. `TestEnsureSchema`),\\n  each test docstring following a `Tests:` / `How:` / `Why:` structure. `os.kill` is patched via `pytest-mock`'s\\n  `MockerFixture` for liveness checks \u2014 analogous pattern available for mocking time-based eviction/TTL checks.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_sqlite_backend.py` covers the other existing SQLite backend\\n  (`backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py`, the 6-table work-item schema) \u2014 useful for WAL-mode and\\n  schema-migration test patterns specifically, even though that backend itself must not be reused per the ADR.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/unit/progressive_markdown/` holds the existing\\n  `progressive_markdown` unit tests (`test_ambiguous_section_ref.py`, `test_indexer_decomposition.py`,\\n  `test_init_docstring.py`, `test_navigation_result_unification.py`) \u2014 this is where new control-set-integration\\n  tests for the Navigation stage belong, alongside `tests_sam/test_progressive_markdown.py` (SAM-level\\n  integration tests for the same package, a separate directory).\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] A paginated response returns a stable identifier derived from the content it paginates\\n- [ ] A later page is requested with that identifier plus a page selector or address\\n- [ ] Serving a later page does not re-collect from the provider and does not re-parse\\n- [ ] A request whose identifier no longer matches current content is reported stale, not served\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Open Decisions\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCache scope (session-lived or persisted) and whether the identifier derives from raw markdown or the parsed tree are recorded as open questions in the contract.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"fadcec7bc9250f6f293237e4bffdc234fb5dcee74274d3d3a6fca7ab22c6250c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPx5qWg\"}"}